--- R1
+++ R2
@@ -53,2 +53,22 @@
   _hook_: '*'
+# R2 change (C-001): warn-only loop breaker. R1 evidence: 11/27 failures
+# exited budget_exceeded at the 80-step cap (+1 error), and the dominant shape
+# is a BYTE-IDENTICAL Bash command repeated consecutively with no change of
+# approach (max consecutive-identical run: 015=21, 1653=25, 191=12, 118=11).
+# The agent re-issues the same failing command instead of diagnosing it,
+# burning the whole budget. This reuses harnessx's existing LoopDetectionProcessor
+# but configured WARN-ONLY: it appends an advisory to the tool result after 3
+# byte-identical consecutive calls, telling the agent to change approach, and
+# NEVER raises (threshold=999). The hard-raise is disabled because 3 currently-
+# passing tasks (878/890/505) also repeat identical commands deliberately and a
+# raise would convert those passes into loop_detected failures. Name-only
+# Strategy 2 is disabled (name_warn_threshold=999) because every call is Bash,
+# so name-only would fire on essentially every task.
+- _target_: harnessx.processors.control.loop_detection.LoopDetectionProcessor
+  window_size: 12
+  warn_threshold: 3
+  threshold: 999
+  name_warn_threshold: 999
+  compaction_drop_threshold: 5
+  _hook_: '*'
 # Break max_tokens repetition loops (finish_reason=length, no tool call).